<Layout title="Crawl Space Encapsulation in Nashville, TN" description="Vapor barrier and crawl space encapsulation services for Nashville and Middle Tennessee homes from Dream Solutions Tennessee."><Hero eyebrow="03 / Crawl space encapsulation" title="Better protection.<br />Beneath <em>your feet.</em>" description="A carefully installed vapor barrier helps separate your crawl space from the exposed ground beneath your home." /><section class="split-section"><h2>A better boundary<br /><em>between soil and home.</em></h2><div class="prose"><p>Exposed earth can release moisture into a crawl space. Encapsulation covers the ground with a durable vapor barrier, with attention to seams, edges, and penetrations to limit ground moisture entry.</p><p>A sealed ground covering can also form part of a crawl space radon mitigation system when paired with appropriately designed ventilation beneath the membrane. Encapsulation alone is not a substitute for radon testing or a complete radon mitigation system.</p></div></section><section class="process-section"><p class="eyebrow">What to expect</p><h2>A clear path forward.</h2><div class="process-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">01</span><h3>Look beneath the home</h3><p>Evaluate crawl space conditions and identify moisture or drainage issues that may need attention before sealing.</p></div><div><span class="eyebrow">02</span><h3>Create the barrier</h3><p>Install and seal a vapor barrier around the crawl space’s shape, supports, and penetrations.</p></div><div><span class="eyebrow">03</span><h3>Plan for the whole space</h3><p>Discuss ongoing moisture control and whether a separate radon mitigation system is appropriate. A barrier does not solve every water or humidity issue.</p></div></div></section><CallToAction /></Layout>